 "validation": {
  "mangkhut-2018": [
   {
    "id": "ttu",
    "grade": "B",
    "basis": "沙田区议会文件 STDC 93/2018：渠务署记旧村停车场水深 1 m 以上、警方记旧村最高水位约 1.5 m，议员称「水深超过 1 米」；均非测量",
    "zh": "沙田曾大屋旧村停车场",
    "en": "Tsang Tai Uk old village car park, Sha Tin",
    "lon": 114.1952,
    "lat": 22.37693,
    "nosnap": true,
    "note_zh": "取样点是围屋东侧的旧村停车场低洼处（DTM 5.1–5.3 mPD，四周道路 5.8–6.1），不是 6.0 mPD 的围屋本身。沙田区议会 STDC 93/2018：渠务署称曾大屋旧村是低洼地，雨水不能直接排入附近排水系统，先入蓄洪池再由泵房抽走；议员称当日乡公所对出的渠务署水泵已停运；渠务署记停车场水深 1 m 以上、警方记旧村最高水位约 1.5 m。沙田没有验潮站（渠务署以大埔滘 4.54 mPD 为准；沙田最高十分钟平均风速仅 58 km/h，风壅水 < 0.15 m，模型取 +5% 约 4.65 mPD），河水淹不到 5.1 mPD 的停车场：水来自本地降雨 + 泵停运（v0.8 起作为临时措施建模）",
    "note_en": "Sample point: the low pocket of the old-village car park east of the walled house (DTM 5.1-5.3 mPD, surrounding roads 5.8-6.1), not the 6.0 mPD walled compound. Sha Tin DC paper STDC 93/2018: DSD states the old village is a low-lying spot whose runoff cannot drain directly into the local system but collects in a storage pond and is pumped out; the councillor reported the DSD pump outside the village office had stopped; DSD logged over 1 m in the car park, the Police about 1.5 m. Sha Tin has no tide gauge (DSD refers to Tai Po Kau 4.54 mPD; peak 10-min wind at Sha Tin only 58 km/h, set-up < 0.15 m, model +5% ~ 4.65 mPD): the river cannot reach the 5.1 mPD car park, the water is local rain with the pump down (modelled as a temporary measure from v0.8)",
    "depth": 1.0,
    "cls": "severe",
    "src": "HKO: serious flooding, evacuations",
    "x": 2655.3,
    "y": 1914.7
   },
   {
    "id": "smr",
    "grade": "C",
    "basis": "天文台：单车径与行人隧道被海水淹浸，无深度",
    "zh": "城门河单车径（沙田）",
    "en": "Shing Mun River cycle track",
    "lon": 114.19704,
    "lat": 22.38669,
    "nosnap": true,
    "berm": 3.5,
    "depth": 0.7,
    "cls": "moderate",
    "src": "HKO: inundated cycle tracks & subways",
    "note_zh": "城门河西岸（沙田公园以北）。单车径阶地不在数据里：CEDD LiDAR 在河道走廊无回波、LandsD 填成 5.27 mPD 平面，10 m 格与 1 m 分位数都没有阶地。按沙田区议会文件 ST 2018/094（河堤即单车径约 3–6 mPD、河边长廊 2.6 mPD 以上）取阶地 3.5 mPD：模拟值 = 模型在此处的河道峰值水位 − 3.5，即只检验沙田的潮位推算，不是地表水动力。v0.8 前此点误放在西侧 300 m 外的明渠旁",
    "note_en": "West bank north of Sha Tin Park. The cycle-track berm is absent from the data (no LiDAR returns over the river corridor, LandsD fill at a flat 5.27 mPD, neither the 10 m cell nor the 1 m quantiles hold it). Berm taken as 3.5 mPD from Sha Tin DC paper ST 2018/094 (cycle-track embankment about 3-6 mPD, promenade 2.6 mPD or above): sim = peak modelled river level here minus 3.5, i.e. a test of the Sha Tin tide estimate, not of surface hydraulics. Before v0.8 the point sat 300 m west beside a nullah",
    "x": 2844.7,
    "y": 2995.5
   }
  ],
